The points A, B, C have position vectors $\boldsymbol{i}+\boldsymbol{j}+2\boldsymbol{k}$, $\boldsymbol{i}+2\boldsymbol{j}+3\boldsymbol{k}$, $3\boldsymbol{i}+\boldsymbol{k}$ respectively and lie in the plane $\pi$.
(a) Find
(i) the area of the triangle ABC;
(ii) the shortest distance from C to the line AB;
(iii) the cartesian equation of the plane $\pi$. [14 marks]
The line $L$ passes through the origin and is normal to the plane $\pi$, it intersects $\pi$ at the point D.
(b) Find
(i) the coordinates of the point D;
(ii) the distance of $\pi$ from the origin. [6 marks]
